bitcoin's price has been dropping  aggressively over the last eight months  or so now of course it's important first  let's zoom out if we go ahead and we  zoom out what we can see here on the  price is that bitcoin is up a lot over a  long period of time but again over the  last eight months you can see that  bitcoin has fallen from 69 000 back in  november all the way today to about 23  300  now many people are worried about the  price and they should be that's the  thing that moves on a day-to-day basis  but there is a difference between price  and value price is the thing that people  are willing to trade on a daily basis  but value is actually what is going to  hold over the long period of time if  it's a good asset during these times  when price is falling it's always  important to re-evaluate your investment  thesis is bitcoin as an open source  decentralized digital currency with a  programmatic monetary policy and a  finite supply still valuable or has that  value come down with price if it hasn't  that just means that price and value are  diverging and ultimately it's  undervalued but that is important to  actually go look at the underlying  fundamentals before we can make that  conclusion so let's jump right in and  take a first look at hash rate with the  hash rate what we can see is that it has  quadrupled over the last three years  this shows that bitcoin is more secure  today than it has been ever before if we  then take a look at the average  transaction fee paid on layer 1 of  bitcoin we can see that today it's under  a dollar and 50 cents that means that it  is incredibly cheap to go ahead and make  very large transfers of value but more  importantly you can see back in 2017  there was a huge spike in fees when  bitcoin hit an all-time high at 20 000  and then in q1 and q2 of 2021 the first  time we hit a new all-time high we saw a  big spike in fees as well but as you'll  notice from this chart as we entered  into the latter half of 2021 even though  price went back and hit a new all-time  high of 69 000 there was no large  increase in fees that's because there's  been tons of innovation on layer one and  also a very large rise in the adoption  of the lightning network then if we take  a look at the on-chain distribution of  bitcoin we can see that there are wallet  addresses holding .01 bitcoin point one  bitcoin and one bitcoin all hitting  all-time highs these small players in  the bitcoin market they continue to  dollar cost average they continue to  suck up economic value and it's actually  the whales the large holders of bitcoin  that are selling well the little guys  the plebs they're the ones who are  buying up all that bitcoin then we can  take a look at long-term versus  short-term holders and will clemente  pointing out that we are watching the  short-term holder cost bases actually  drop at the same time the long-term  holder cost basis is rising historically  when these two things have crossed and  the short-term holder cost basis has  gone below the long-term holder cost  basis it has signaled a very very  attractive price point next up we can  look at transaction metrics and when we  look here at the active addresses we can  see that even though price has been  drawing down the number of active  addresses is still in line and within  the range that we have seen historically  the same is also true of the number of  transactions on the network as well we  continue to see the number of  transactions showing right within that  same exact range we can see here that  the number of transactions continue to  show right within that historical range  as well  next up we can take a look at the  percent of bitcoin in circulating supply  that's in profit we're now under 52 of  bitcoin in circulation actually in  profit that may seem low compared to  historical norms but unfortunately  usually we see under 50 percent in bear  markets and so somewhere in that 40 to  45 range something to keep an eye out  and then lastly the lightning network  capacity continues to reach all-time  high levels as well and it just seems to  be growing like a weed up and to the  right  now of course nobody knows what's going  to happen the federal reserve is in  control right now they are tanking asset  prices across markets by raising  interest rates and conducting  quantitative tightening  all assets are one trade at the moment  but what is important for you as an  investor to do is take a look at what's  happening with the price be aware of it  pay attention to it but also understand  what the underlying fundamentals are are  you actually seeing the fundamentals  degrade are they getting worse or is  this simply price diverging from the  value of an asset now of course when i  go and i re-evaluate i revisit my  investment thesis over the weekend i  come to the same conclusion bitcoin is  not only continuing to be adopted it's  not only doing exactly what it was  supposed to do but it's actually  reaching all-time highs and a number of  these underlying fundamentals that makes  me very confident that bitcoin is still  in the exact same place that it was  before the price started to fall now the  price could go down more or maybe not i  don't know what's going to happen but  what i do know is that price and value  seem to be diverging and if you're a  long-term holder you simply want to  understand what the value of the asset  is not necessarily the price i hope this  is helpful as you continue to break down  bitcoin and what you're going to do over  the coming months but understand the  difference between price and value is  important in every asset and bitcoin is  no different hey you did you like this  video great we make five of them a day  and post them here on this channel make  sure you subscribe like the video and  see you next time

